bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    u8_array_into_word_array_residual_shapes_2026-11-28, 0, "Follow-up to u8_array_into_word_array_unchecked_slots_2026-11-28 (shapes 1, 2 and 4 confirmed by a compile probe on the fixed seed; 3 and 5 by reading the helpers). The E1003 [u8]-into-word-array rule (reject_array_element_mismatch, src/compiler_rust/compiler/src/hir/lower/module_lowering/function.rs) still admits: (1) an optional VALUE: a `[u8]?` into a `[i64]?` slot (is_u8_array_value does not look through the value's Option), (2) a later-declared callee or method parameter spelled `Option<[i64]>` (numeric_array_param_element peels only the `[T]?` spelling), (3) a trait-typed receiver that is not a local (`self.store.put(b)`): trait_method_param_rows resolves locals only, (4) a `[u8]` pushed into a `[[i64]]` with the builtin push/append, (5) untyped list relays. Also note: the assignment slot fires on a local whose word-array type is INFERRED (e.g. `var out = text.bytes()`, typed [i64] by the seed, then `out = helper_returning_u8(out)`); five in-tree buffers were annotated `[u8]` for it. Owner question: keep that, or restrict the assignment slot to declared types."

